historic-routing (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=low

  * @KIND_CHANGELOG@.
    Native Debian 13 package build.
    Source commit: @COMMIT@.
    FRR baseline: @FRR_COMMIT@.
  * Package split: historic-routing-runtime (libfrr.so.0, zebra, vtysh,
    configuration skeleton) and historic-routing-egp (egpd + its unit).
  * Both packages are bound to one build: exact version dependency
    plus the historic-routing-abi marker @ABI@.
    Raw identity: @ABI_RAW@ (the leading "0." exists only because
    Debian version numbers must start with a digit).
  * Installed under /opt/historic-routing/<FRR short commit>/; the
    distribution FRR (/etc/frr, /usr/sbin/frr*, frr.service, libfrr in
    /usr/lib) is not modified.
  * Sockets and PID files live in @RUNSTATEDIR@ (systemd
    RuntimeDirectory), not in the install prefix.
  * Services are installed but neither enabled nor started.
  * RUNPATH of the shipped binaries is $ORIGIN/../lib, so libfrr is loaded only
    from this project's own prefix.

 -- Chenlang Li <Cc1580155hsg@163.com>  @DATE@
